1
00:00:04,722 --> 00:00:07,069
Whiskers and the Swan Castle.

2
00:00:15,769 --> 00:00:20,238
One rainy autumn afternoon, Pip found a treasure in the attic.

3
00:00:24,216 --> 00:00:25,835
Look! An old storybook!

4
00:00:26,035 --> 00:00:29,112
The Swan Castle. It looks like a castle from a dream!

5
00:00:29,312 --> 00:00:34,480
Look at the stamp. Neuschwanstein Castle Library. Please return by eighteen eighty-six!

6
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,689
That's not late. That's ancient.

7
00:00:36,889 --> 00:00:40,899
The last page is torn out! Let's take it back, and find out how it ends.

8
00:00:41,099 --> 00:00:43,310
To the mountains? No, thank you.

9
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:46,606
Bavaria. Land of giant pretzels and apple strudel.

10
00:00:49,639 --> 00:00:51,033
I'll get the box.

11
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:57,322
So Pip packed the book, and the two cats with it.

12
00:00:57,522 --> 00:01:00,425
A box and a long ride. Best trip ever.

13
00:01:04,875 --> 00:01:06,896
Oops. That stamp was for the box.

14
00:01:19,374 --> 00:01:22,972
All night, the yellow post van drove south, to Munich.

15
00:01:34,505 --> 00:01:37,740
Munich! Look, the little figures on the tower are dancing!

16
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:40,989
Never mind dancing. I smell pretzels!

17
00:01:53,467 --> 00:01:55,997
Servus! Is this runaway pretzel yours?

18
00:01:56,197 --> 00:02:00,109
I let it roll on purpose. Pretzels need exercise.

19
00:02:00,309 --> 00:02:02,739
I'm Resi! Where are you going with that big book?

20
00:02:02,939 --> 00:02:05,006
To the Swan Castle, to give it back!

21
00:02:05,206 --> 00:02:07,900
That's my forest! Hop on Hansl's hay wagon!

22
00:02:18,016 --> 00:02:22,275
Hansl the horse pulled them to a village of painted houses.

23
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:25,766
Nobody passes our village without trying the apple strudel!

24
00:02:35,411 --> 00:02:39,179
A cream beard. On purpose. It's Bavarian fashion.

25
00:02:39,379 --> 00:02:44,605
And relax, Luna. From now on, I'll carry the book. I'm very responsible.

26
00:02:53,777 --> 00:02:57,705
Beyond the village lay the deep, dark Bavarian forest.

27
00:03:02,155 --> 00:03:04,526
Resi? Why do the trees have eyes?

28
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,859
Those are only deer, silly. Say hello!

29
00:03:21,698 --> 00:03:24,555
The Swan Castle! Even more beautiful than in the book!

30
00:03:24,755 --> 00:03:27,152
Behold! Sir Whiskers, the Swan Knight!

31
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:37,508
I dropped it on purpose. To see if books can fly.

32
00:03:37,708 --> 00:03:41,198
Whiskers. That book waited a hundred and forty years to go home.

33
00:03:45,648 --> 00:03:49,858
No. It wasn't on purpose. I was showing off. It was my fault.

34
00:04:01,392 --> 00:04:02,717
Pull, everybody!

35
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,609
You did it! It's soggy, but safe!

36
00:04:17,365 --> 00:04:21,501
Good evening. I am Ludwig, keeper of the castle library.

37
00:04:21,701 --> 00:04:24,527
We came to return a book. It's a tiny bit late.

38
00:04:24,727 --> 00:04:28,205
The Swan Castle! Welcome home, old friend!

39
00:04:28,405 --> 00:04:31,910
It's wet because I dropped it. My fault. I'm sorry.

40
00:04:35,416 --> 00:04:39,573
Telling the truth when it's hard? That is what a true knight does.

41
00:04:39,773 --> 00:04:44,364
And the last page? It was never written. Perhaps you should write it.

42
00:04:56,842 --> 00:05:00,450
And they all ate apple strudel, happily ever after.

43
00:05:00,650 --> 00:05:03,778
And the cat told the truth. That was the bravest thing of all.

44
00:05:11,533 --> 00:05:15,906
A perfect ending. Now, home you go. Return to sender!

45
00:05:24,606 --> 00:05:26,402
You're back! How does the story end?

46
00:05:26,602 --> 00:05:32,560
We wrote it ourselves! And the cat said, it was my fault. And everybody still loved him.

47
00:05:37,482 --> 00:05:42,522
Because anyone can make a mistake. The truly brave say: that was me.

